From c29105a4ce6772fddf5721e24afdb47a15637540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:04:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: global tangent operator with the pattern and the
 exchanges kept

In parallel, the tangent operator assembled by kernels was built at each
assembly as the product P^T A P of hypre (block diagonal matrix of the
local matrices, prolongation of the true degrees of freedom), which
computes again the pattern and the communications. On 8 processes, this
product cost more than the assembly of the local matrices by kernels.

batch::GlobalStiffnessMatrix: when each row of the prolongation has a
single entry, equal to one (conforming spaces), each entry of the local
matrix goes to a fixed entry of the global matrix. The first assembly
computes the pattern of the global matrix (product of hypre on a matrix of
ones), the position of each local entry in the part of the global matrix
owned by the process or its place in the message to the owner of its row,
and the positions of the received entries; the following ones only copy,
exchange (MPI_Alltoallv) and add the values. Used by the tangent operator
assembled by kernels when hypre does not use the GPU; otherwise, the
product of hypre is kept.

On 8 processes: 2.5 ms instead of 15.4 ms for linear tetrahedra in
mechanics, 1.7 ms instead of 36.8 ms in heat transfer, same matrices.
